section(1,'Completion overview')
story.append(p('This report records the platform updates delivered by SpectreTech Limited in response to the client\'s September 2026 meeting requests. It covers membership, finance, projects, access permissions, family management, public communications and meeting administration.'))
box('Status at issue','All requested changes and previously outstanding implementation tasks are complete. M-Pesa integration is prepared; activation remains dependent on the client supplying the required M-Pesa details.')
section(2,'Membership standing')
bullets(['Members now have an automatic <b>Paid up</b> or <b>Lapsed</b> standing. Monthly fees fall due at month-end; unpaid balances trigger a lapse after the following month\'s grace period. Annual subscriptions follow their renewal window.','Admin can configure the monthly fee, grace period (default 15 days), annual fee and annual renewal window (default 45 days) under Finance settings.','A member is reactivated automatically when payment covers the amount owed. Admin can manually override standing, with an optional expiry date.','Attached family members inherit their Principal Member\'s standing. Admin and Super Admin retain access.','Lapsed members can log in and view past events and the gallery; upcoming events and projects are restricted. Standing is updated hourly and when payments are recorded.'])
section(3,'Payment purposes and campaigns')
bullets(['The Treasurer can manage payment purposes, including Monthly Contribution, Annual Subscription, Funeral, Registration and Project. Monthly, Annual or None classifications support membership standing and reporting.','Campaigns are available when recording payments and support an overall target plus an optional per-member target. They can be edited, deactivated and reactivated, with past start dates supported.','Treasurer campaign pages show progress, individual member contributions and waive/undo controls. Newly approved members are automatically added to open campaigns. Admin Finance uses the same campaign form.'])
page()
section(4,'Contribution history and financial reporting')
bullets(['Contribution history includes Member and Purpose filters, a Purpose column and the month covered by each payment. Monthly contributions default to the payment month.','The new <b>Active months</b> report includes Excel/CSV export and is available to Treasurer, Admin, Executive and Auditor roles.','Monthly payments cover the applicable fee, with excess amounts carried into later months. A full annual subscription covers 12 months.','Loan disbursement requires additional approval only when the amount is strictly above the configured threshold.'])
section(5,'Project management')
bullets(['Projects now include start and end dates. Status changes automatically to Planned, Active or Completed according to the schedule in Nairobi time, with hourly updates.','Funding progress reflects actual money raised against the target: investments plus confirmed contributions linked to the project. The public project page uses the same calculation.','Contributions and expenses can be linked to projects so spending is tracked per project. The management panel presents separate Funding progress and Schedule sections.'])
section(6,'Roles and access permissions')
bullets(['The Organizer role is now labelled <b>Organizing Secretary</b> throughout the platform. The Secretary can manage events from the Secretary menu.','Only Super Admin can appoint an Admin or change an Admin\'s role or dashboard access. Roles &amp; access includes a Principal Member toggle.','The Auditor redirect issue has been resolved. Auditor access is read-only for financial reports and exports, member statement and receipt PDFs, documents and downloads, governance records and attachments, meetings and reports, and the full member directory.','Voting controls are hidden for the Auditor. Document management is limited to Admin and Secretary; Organizing Secretary document-management access has been removed.'])
page()
section(7,'Family and Principal Member management')
bullets(['Only Admin and Super Admin can transfer an attached member to another Principal Member.','Lineage has been removed from registration, member profiles, Family &amp; Branch, family administration, the directory, member tables, approvals and loan details. It remains optional and appears only in the Admin member export.','The Admin dashboard chart now shows <b>Members per Principal</b>.'])
section(8,'About Us profiles and Contact Us')
bullets(['A new <b>Communications &gt; About Us profiles</b> page lets Admin link executives to member records and maintain display names, titles, responsibilities, biographies, photo URLs and display order. Profiles can be published or kept as drafts.','The public About page displays published executives with their responsibilities and biographies. Members control whether their photo, profession, location, email and phone may appear through Public profile settings.','Contact enquiries can reach multiple recipients. Admin can maintain an Also send to list under Contact &amp; finance settings. If empty, active Secretaries, Treasurers and Executives receive copies.','Notification copies are sent separately so an invalid recipient address does not block the main notification.'])
section(9,'Meetings, support and module availability')
bullets(['The minutes editor supports member search and Present, Apology and Absent attendance statuses. Invited members are pre-listed, totals are calculated automatically, and Mark all present is available. Guest and historical attendance text fields remain supported.','PDF, Word and bulk meeting exports, together with Meetings &amp; reports, show the combined attendance records.','Executives can respond to member support chats and receive email alerts alongside Admin and Super Admin. Conversation deletion remains Admin-only.','When Loans or Welfare is switched off, the eight affected pages show a clear disabled-page message and a dashboard link.'])
page()
section(10,'M-Pesa integration readiness')
bullets(['One configurable M-Pesa integration supports sandbox and production, with PayBill or Buy Goods collection options. Transaction timestamps use Nairobi time.','STK payment requests can specify a payment purpose, campaign, project or contribution month. Confirmed payments are recorded against the selected allocation.','STK initiation remains restricted to Treasurer and Admin until the required M-Pesa credentials are supplied and activation is completed.','Configuration examples and operational guidance cover PayBill versus Buy Goods, activation steps and a live KES 1 STK verification.'])
section(11,'Documentation, database and delivery')
bullets(['Project documentation has been updated to record the September meeting changes and the associated operating procedures.','The live database migration adds membership standing and override fields, public-profile settings, payment-purpose classifications, per-member campaign targets, project-linked contributions, committee profile links and responsibilities, and member-based meeting attendance. Default payment purposes are included.','Existing campaign targets have been converted to overall totals while preserving the previous per-member amount.','The previously outstanding deployment, manual browser checks, scheduled-job configuration and other launch preparation items have been resolved.'])
